{
	"_note": "Dungeons are chains of events; events are shared and each dungeon scales them. Dungeon: 'minutes' is the whole run (events are spread evenly, then the walk home), 'chooser' is who picks options (player / timeout / policy), 'max_party' 0 = any size, 'difficulty' multiplies option difficulty, 'danger' multiplies how many are lost, 'loot' multiplies coins, 'box' is the box type found and the odds for part rarity. Option: 'stat' is tested against 'difficulty' with the party's total (empty = always works), 'tag' is for future policies, 'min_party' hides it for smaller parties. Outcome: 'lost'/'injured'/'heal' are [min, max] fractions of the party, 'coins' is per pet still there, 'box_chance'/'part_chance' grow with the square root of the party, 'progress' is continue / end / skip, 'leave_injured' leaves the injured behind. {who} is the pet's name, or 'the party'.",
